//
// Description : The per-file Rename dialog behind the board's overriding-copies line - one row per
//               workspace copy standing in front of a DataFlex system package, a tick per row, and
//               the two facts that decide the tick: whether THIS build compiled the copy, and
//               whether it is byte-identical to the shipped file.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use Windows.pkg
Use Cursor.pkg
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg      // tShadowCopy, eShadow*, the CS_Ico* icon names
Use cRefactorApplication.pkg
Use cFTModalPanel.pkg         // FT: the dark modal, same base as BackupFilesFT.dg
Use cFTCJSelectionGrid.pkg    // the checkbox grid the Undo dialog and the copy-scope picker use
Use FTAllWebControlClasses.pkg   // FT: cFTWebButton - the two button bars - and cFTWebHtmlBox, the note
Use cFTLocalWebControlHost.pkg   // FT: hosts the note band
Use cFTGridHost.pkg              // FT: the two button bars - hosts on a grid (RDCFlexTron)
Use FTMarkupBuilders.pkg         // the HTML vocabulary - DivOpen, CssLink - for the note
Use FTThemeColors.pkg            // FTWebBg / FTThemeInk - the FT palette
Use FTMessageBox.pkg             // FTStopBox (RDCFlexTron)

// What a press of Recommended does - on the button, and set again by RefreshFooterAndButtons whenever the button
// is open. While a press would change nothing the button is shut and its tooltip says why instead.
Define CS_RetireRecommendedTip for "Back to the recommended ticks: every copy a rename cannot cost anything is ticked - the ones byte-identical to the file they stand in front of, the ones that differ but add nothing the workspace uses, plus errornum.inc, an incomplete copy that starves the real one - and the rest are unticked."

/*  WHY A DIALOG WITH A TICK PER FILE (Nils 2026-09-15).

    Until today the board's [Rename them] renamed every overriding copy behind one confirm. That was
    right for the population it was built on - copies of DataFlex system files, decades old, strict
    subsets of the installed file - and wrong for the population that arrived with it: the
    workspace's own copies of files its LIBRARIES ship. Measured on five workspaces, one to five
    such copies each, and EVERY one differed from the library's file - an older version of the
    library's own package, compiled in its place. Renaming those blind would break a build per fork.
    Nils: "we probably need to suggest this on a file-by-file basis" - and both kinds now come here,
    the install line included ("Yes, move the install line to the same per-file dialog").

    THE TICK IS DECIDED BY THE CONTENT. A copy byte-identical to the shipped file is pure redundancy
    and starts ticked; a copy that differs is a fork until someone looks and starts unticked. The
    grid shows both facts per row - which file it stands in front of, whether this build compiled
    it, identical or DIFFERENT - so the user decides with the evidence in front of them rather than
    from a sentence in a confirm. Select All / None / Invert and Recommended are the bulk verbs;
    the Space bar toggles the row under the cursor, as in every selection grid here.

    SHAPED LIKE SelectCopyScopeFT / BackupFilesFT: a web select bar above a cFTCJSelectionGrid,
    a note band and a web closer row below it, dark surface throughout. The array is the truth and
    the grid renders it (RenderRows); a tick is copied back by PATH (SyncSelectionFromGrid), never by
    index, because the grid can be sorted by any column.

    FRAMEWORK BUTTONS IN BOTH BARS (2026-09-30): cFTWebButtons on grid hosts (RDCFlexTron), where the
    bars were HTML chips. A button that works on the grid does it inside the click (an OnClick override);
    a closer's own work runs after the click (OnButtonClick), where a message box or Close_Panel is safe.

    SYSTEM PACKAGES ONLY (Nils 2026-10-05, looking at this dialog: "It is actually perfectly OK with
    duplicate filenames, as long as they are not a DataFlex system package. Thus all other 'duplicates'
    should be removed from the dialog"). The copies of library files described above are no longer
    handed to it - the board's memo asks for the system-package copies only - and the "Stands in front
    of" column went with them: every row would have said "DataFlex's own file".

    ONE KIND OF LIBRARY-FILE COPY CAME BACK (2026-11-12): a copy the last build compiled in place of
    the file of a package that has errors in the same build (cShadowedPackageFiles.FailingPackageCopies).
    Its row says so in "This build" - "compiled; VDFQuery20 has errors" - and its tick follows the same
    content rule as every other row.

    A DIFFERENT COPY THAT ADDS NOTHING USED COMES TICKED (Nils 2026-11-12): "DIFFERENT - adds nothing
    used" under Content, when no name it declares beyond the shipped file is used anywhere else in the
    workspace. The board asks before the dialog opens (cShadowedPackageFiles.MarkCopiesThatAddNothingUsed).

    TWO WAYS OUT, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS WHAT HAPPENS TO THE UNTICKED (Nils 2026-09-15, after the
    first live press: "one conundrum on what to do with files that were NOT ticked? I choosed one file
    to be unticked and that makes the 'Rename them...' button to stick"). [Rename N ticked] renames the
    ticked and leaves the rest on the board's line, to be looked at later. [Rename N, keep the other M]
    renames the ticked AND records the unticked as KEPT for this workspace - the user's explicit
    verdict that those are their forks - so they leave the line and the dialog; the line's "M kept"
    chip lists them and offers them again. Nothing is ever inferred: a copy renamed back by hand is
    simply offered again, as before (the inferred skip was dropped the same day). */

Object oRetireShadows_dg is a cFTModalPanel
    Set Label to "Rename the overriding copies"
    Set Size to 252 700
    Set Location to 2 0
    Set piMinSize to 208 560
    Set Icon to "DFRefactor.ico"

    /* THE ROWS, in and out. Set by ChooseShadowCopiesToRetire before Popup; read back with bTicked
       filled once the user has pressed Rename. A struct ARRAY survives a cross-object Get; a bare
       struct would not (see SelectCopyScopeFT). */
    Property tShadowCopy[] paRows
    Property Boolean pbConfirmed False
    // True when the user pressed the "keep the other M" closer: the caller records every unticked
    // row as kept. False after "Rename N ticked" - the unticked stay on the line.
    Property Boolean pbKeepRest False

    /* THE SELECT BAR: the bulk verbs, framework buttons (cFTWebButton, RDCFlexTron) on a grid host of 8 px
       columns, as DeepScanRulesFT's. Each works on the grid INSIDE the click - an OnClick override, then
       Forward - as the chips' OnClick did: the grid op is quick, and a grid read from the click relay's timer
       faults (err 98). Spans fit the captions (Recommended ~123 px, Select All ~91, Select None ~107, Invert
       ~73, measured 2026-09-30); column 56 takes the rest of the width. */
    Object oWebSelectBar is a cFTGridHost
        Set Location to 5 14
        Set Size to 20 672
        Set peAnchors to anTopLeftRight
        Set piColumnCount to 57         // Recommended's 17, Select All's 13, Select None's 15, Invert's 11, then column 56
        Set psColumnWidths to "56/1fr"  // column 56 takes the extra width

        Object oRecommendedBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 0
            Set piColumnSpan to 17
            Set psCaption to "Recommended"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-check"
            Set psToolTip to CS_RetireRecommendedTip

            Procedure OnClick
                Send TickIdenticalOnly of oRetireShadows_dg
                Forward Send OnClick
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oSelectAllBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 17
            Set piColumnSpan to 13
            Set psCaption to "Select All"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-selectall"

            Procedure OnClick
                Send SelectAll of oShadows_grd
                Send AfterGridSelectionChanged of oRetireShadows_dg
                Forward Send OnClick
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oSelectNoneBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 30
            Set piColumnSpan to 15
            Set psCaption to "Select None"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-selectnone"

            Procedure OnClick
                Send SelectNone of oShadows_grd
                Send AfterGridSelectionChanged of oRetireShadows_dg
                Forward Send OnClick
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oInvertBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 45
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "Invert"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-invert"

            Procedure OnClick
                Send SelectInvert of oShadows_grd
                Send AfterGridSelectionChanged of oRetireShadows_dg
                Forward Send OnClick
            End_Procedure
        End_Object
    End_Object

    Object oShadows_grd is a cFTCJSelectionGrid
        Set Location to 29 14
        Set Size to 150 672
        Set peAnchors to anAll
        // A footer row: "N of M ticked" under the file column (RefreshFooterAndButtons).
        Set pbShowFooter to True

        Object oCJGridColumnRowIndicator is a cCJGridColumnRowIndicator
            Set piWidth to 24
            Set pbResizable to False
        End_Object

        Object oFile_col is a cCJGridColumn
            Set piWidth to 150
            Set psCaption to "File"
        End_Object

        Object oBuild_col is a cCJGridColumn
            Set piWidth to 175
            Set psCaption to "This build"
            Set psToolTip to "Whether the last compile read the workspace's copy in place of the shipped file. A copy it did not read compiles nothing today and wins the day the compiler reaches it. A copy of a package's file is listed only when the build compiled it and that package has errors in the same build."
        End_Object

        Object oContent_col is a cCJGridColumn
            Set piWidth to 150
            Set psCaption to "Content"
            Set psToolTip to "identical: the same bytes as the shipped file - renaming it loses nothing. DIFFERENT: a fork until you compare the two. DIFFERENT - adds nothing used: nothing in the workspace uses a name it declares beyond the shipped file, so it is ticked for you; a change inside a method both files have is not seen. DIFFERENT - retire anyway: named as a copy that starves the shipped file rather than forking it, so it is ticked for you."
        End_Object

        Object oPath_col is a cCJGridColumn
            // The IDENTITY column - the selection grid reads phoData_Col to say which rows are
            // ticked, and the full path is the only value here that is unique per row.
            Set phoData_Col to Self
            Set piWidth to 400              // 340, plus the 175 of the "Stands in front of" column that went, less 50 for "This build" and 65 for "Content"
            Set psCaption to "Workspace copy"
            Set psToolTip to "The copy in the workspace. It carries the name of a package DataFlex ships, or of a file of a package that has errors in the last build, and it is what the compiler reaches first."
        End_Object

        /* THE designed fill point. cFTCJSelectionGrid declares an empty LoadData and calls it
           from its own Activating - the one moment the COM control exists and the panel is up. A
           render from the DIALOG's Activate finds nothing to render into (see SelectCopyScopeFT). */
        Procedure LoadData
            Send RenderRows of (Parent(Self))
        End_Procedure

        /* A SINGLE tick, mouse or keyboard. The grid's own RefreshSelectionUpdate only fires from
           the bulk verbs, and DoSetCheckboxFooterText is the one thing both ToggleCurrentItem and
           OnComMouseUp send. Sync + repaint the closer only - NOT RenderRows, which re-initialises
           the grid underneath the click still being handled. */
        Procedure DoSetCheckboxFooterText
            Forward Send DoSetCheckboxFooterText
            Send SyncSelectionFromGrid of (Parent(Self))
            Send RefreshFooterAndButtons of (Parent(Self))
        End_Procedure
    End_Object

    /* THE NOTE BAND - the three facts the old confirm carried, now under the list they apply to:
       what a rename does and how it is undone, why a DIFFERENT copy starts unticked, and that
       nothing here is remembered as an exception. Prose, not a control. */
    Object oWebNoteBar is a cFTLocalWebControlHost
        Set Location to 183 14
        Set Size to 30 672
        Set peAnchors to anBottomLeftRight

        Function NoteHtml Returns String
            String sHtml
            Move (CS_PaletteCssLink + CS_PageFitCssLink + CssLink("retireshadows")) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (DivOpen("rsnote")) ;
                + 'A ticked file is copied to the backup area, then renamed to <b>&lt;name&gt;.shadowed</b> ' ;
                + 'so the next build reads the shipped file - <b>Revert</b> restores it, and so does renaming it back. ' ;
                + 'A copy marked <b>DIFFERENT</b> starts unticked: it may be a fork the code depends on, and the next ' ;
                + 'build that reaches the shipped file will fail if it was - compare the two first. ' ;
                + 'One exception is ticked for you: <b>errornum.inc</b>, shown as <b>DIFFERENT - retire anyway</b>. ' ;
                + 'A workspace copy of it does not fork the constants, it STARVES them - its include guard stops the ' ;
                + 'real file loading, so every constant the old copy never had comes back undefined. Untick it like ' ;
                + 'any other if you disagree. ' ;
                + '<b>Rename</b> leaves the unticked on the board for later; <b>keep the other</b> records them as ' ;
                + 'forks, off the board until its "kept" chip offers them again. A copy renamed back by hand is offered again.' ;
                + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml
            Function_Return sHtml
        End_Function

        Object oWebNote_htm is a cFTWebHtmlBox
            Set piColumnSpan  to 1
            Set pbServerOnClick to False
            // DESIGN-TIME PLACEHOLDER for the Studio's Windows Designer, which models the LAST literal
            // psHtml it can parse. It is the string the runtime seeds (dumped by the cFTWebHtmlBox design
            // dump, no workspace loaded); the runtime expression sits in End_Construct_Object below.
            Set psHtml to """
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/palette.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/buttons.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/bars.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/pagefit.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="CssStyle/retireshadows.css">
            <div class="rsnote">A ticked file is copied to the backup area, then renamed to <b>&lt;name&gt;.shadowed</b> so the next build reads the shipped file - <b>Revert</b> restores it, and so
                does renaming it back. A copy marked <b>DIFFERENT</b> starts unticked: it may be a fork the code depends on, and the next build that reaches the shipped file will fail if it was -
                compare the two first. One exception is ticked for you: <b>errornum.inc</b>, shown as <b>DIFFERENT - retire anyway</b>. A workspace copy of it does not fork the constants, it STARVES
                them - its include guard stops the real file loading, so every constant the old copy never had comes back undefined. Untick it like any other if you disagree. <b>Rename</b> leaves the
                unticked on the board for later; <b>keep the other</b> records them as forks, off the board until its "kept" chip offers them again. A copy renamed back by hand is offered again.</div>
            """

            // RUNTIME content - here rather than in the object body, so the Designer keeps the literal above.
            Procedure End_Construct_Object
                Forward Send End_Construct_Object
                Set psHtml to (NoteHtml(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object
    End_Object

    /* THE CLOSER ROW. Two verbs that differ only in what happens to the UNTICKED rows, each naming its
       counts, and each shut when it has nothing to act on, with the reason in its tooltip - a button that
       looks dead must be dead (the SelectCopyScopeFT rule). "Keep" alone, with nothing ticked, is a
       legitimate press: the user has compared every copy and is keeping the lot. Not now is never shut.

       Framework buttons (cFTWebButton, RDCFlexTron) since 2026-09-30. Their captions carry the counts, so
       each has a column as wide as its caption (max-content, with ftbtn-fit's 76 px least - the message
       box's answers' layout), and column 0 takes the rest; RefreshFooterAndButtons sets the captions and
       states. A closer syncs the ticks from the grid INSIDE the click (OnClick, then Forward) - a grid read
       from the click relay's timer faults (err 98) - and its OnButtonClick runs DoConfirm or DoCancel after
       the click, where a message box and Close_Panel are safe. The chips did both inside the click. */
    Object oWebBottomBar is a cFTGridHost
        Set Location to 218 14
        Set Size to 20 672
        Set peAnchors to anBottomLeftRight
        Set piColumnCount to 4
        Set psColumnWidths to "0/1fr 1/max-content 2/max-content 3/max-content"

        Object oRenameBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 1
            Set piColumnSpan to 1
            Set psCaption to "Rename 0 ticked"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftbtn-fit ftg-check"
            Set pbEnabled to False
            Set psToolTip to "Nothing is ticked. Tick the copies to rename, keep the rest, or press Not now."

            Procedure OnClick
                Send SyncSelectionFromGrid of oRetireShadows_dg
                Forward Send OnClick
            End_Procedure

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoConfirm of oRetireShadows_dg False
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oKeepBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 2
            Set piColumnSpan to 1
            Set psCaption to "Keep all 0"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftbtn-fit ftg-check"
            Set pbEnabled to False
            Set psToolTip to "Every copy is ticked - there is nothing to keep."

            Procedure OnClick
                Send SyncSelectionFromGrid of oRetireShadows_dg
                Forward Send OnClick
            End_Procedure

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoConfirm of oRetireShadows_dg True
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oNotNowBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 3
            Set piColumnSpan to 1
            Set psCaption to "Not now"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftbtn-fit ftg-close"
            Set psToolTip to "Close without renaming or keeping anything."

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoCancel of oRetireShadows_dg
            End_Procedure
        End_Object
    End_Object

    // Ticked rows. One function because the footer, the closer row and DoConfirm all ask, and
    // they must never disagree.
    Function TickedCount Returns Integer
        tShadowCopy[] aRows
        Integer i iLast iTicked

        Get paRows to aRows
        Move 0 to iTicked
        Move (SizeOfArray(aRows) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (aRows[i].bTicked = True) ;
                Increment iTicked
        Loop
        Function_Return iTicked
    End_Function

    // The words the fact columns show for a row. Kept short - they are read per row, not once.
    Function BuildText tShadowCopy Row Returns String
        If (Row.eKind = eShadowFailingPackage) ;
            Function_Return ("compiled; " + Row.sSource + " has errors")
        If (Row.iClass = 0) ;
            Function_Return "compiled this copy"
        Function_Return "did not read it"
    End_Function

    Function ContentText tShadowCopy Row Returns String
        If (Row.bSame = True) ;
            Function_Return "identical"
        // A DIFFERENT row that is ticked anyway has to say so, or the tick looks arbitrary
        // against the column beside it.
        If (Row.bAlways = True) ;
            Function_Return "DIFFERENT - retire anyway"
        If (Row.bAddsNothingUsed = True) ;
            Function_Return "DIFFERENT - adds nothing used"
        Function_Return "DIFFERENT"
    End_Function

    /* Render paRows into the grid. One direction only - the array is the truth. GUARDED ON THE COM
       OBJECT: the CodeJock grid does not exist until the dialog is created, and reaching into it
       early raises error 4399, "pvComObject is NULL". */
    Procedure RenderRows
        Handle hoDataSource
        tDataSourceRow[] TheData TheDataEmpty
        tShadowCopy[] aRows
        tShadowCopy Row
        Integer i iLast iFile iBuild iContent iPath iCheck

        If (not(IsComObjectCreated(oShadows_grd))) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Get paRows to aRows
        Get phoDataSource of oShadows_grd to hoDataSource
        If (hoDataSource = 0) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Get DataSource of hoDataSource to TheData
        Move TheDataEmpty to TheData

        Get piColumnId of oFile_col    to iFile
        Get piColumnId of oBuild_col   to iBuild
        Get piColumnId of oContent_col to iContent
        Get piColumnId of oPath_col    to iPath
        Get piColumnId of (phoCheckbox_Col(oShadows_grd)) to iCheck

        Move (SizeOfArray(aRows) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move aRows[i] to Row
            Move Row.sLeaf                 to TheData[i].sValue[iFile]
            Move (BuildText(Self, Row))    to TheData[i].sValue[iBuild]
            Move (ContentText(Self, Row))  to TheData[i].sValue[iContent]
            Move Row.sPath                 to TheData[i].sValue[iPath]
            // A Boolean, not "1"/"0" - the selection grid reads this slot straight back into a
            // Boolean, so the raw value has to be one it wrote itself.
            Move Row.bTicked               to TheData[i].sValue[iCheck]
        Loop

        Send InitializeData of oShadows_grd TheData
        If (iLast >= 0) ;
            Send MoveToFirstRow of oShadows_grd
        Send RefreshFooterAndButtons
    End_Procedure

    /* Copy the grid's tick state back into paRows, matched by PATH. The grid can be sorted by any
       column, so a positional copy would silently assign one file's answer to another. */
    Procedure SyncSelectionFromGrid
        tFolderData[] aGrid
        tShadowCopy[] aRows
        Integer i j iLast jLast

        Get AllItems of oShadows_grd to aGrid
        Get paRows to aRows
        Move (SizeOfArray(aRows) - 1) to iLast
        Move (SizeOfArray(aGrid) - 1) to jLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            For j from 0 to jLast
                If (Lowercase(Trim(aGrid[j].sFolderName)) = Lowercase(Trim(aRows[i].sPath))) ;
                    Move aGrid[j].bSelected to aRows[i].bTicked
            Loop
        Loop
        Set paRows to aRows
    End_Procedure

    // A bulk verb ran on the grid: read its result, then repaint from the array, so the display can
    // never disagree with the answer that will be returned.
    Procedure AfterGridSelectionChanged
        Send SyncSelectionFromGrid
        Send RenderRows
    End_Procedure

    // The recommended answer, re-applied: identical copies ticked, different ones not.
    Procedure TickIdenticalOnly
        tShadowCopy[] aRows
        Integer i iLast

        Get paRows to aRows
        Move (SizeOfArray(aRows) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            // bAlways too: this is the RECOMMENDED answer, and dropping errornum.inc from it
            // would untick the one row whose rename matters most.
            Move (aRows[i].bSame or aRows[i].bAlways or aRows[i].bAddsNothingUsed) to aRows[i].bTicked
        Loop
        Set paRows to aRows
        Send RenderRows
    End_Procedure

    // The footer count, the two closers and Recommended, from the same numbers - every tick path ends here.
    Procedure RefreshFooterAndButtons
        tShadowCopy[] aRows
        Integer iTicked iRows iRest i iRec
        String sRename sKeep sRenameTip sKeepTip sRecTip
        Handle hoBar hoSelBar hoRename hoKeep hoRec
        Boolean bWant bAsRec

        Get TickedCount to iTicked
        Get paRows to aRows
        Move (SizeOfArray(aRows)) to iRows
        Move (iRows - iTicked) to iRest
        If (IsComObjectCreated(oShadows_grd)) ;
            Set psFooterText of oFile_col to (String(iTicked) + " of " + String(iRows) + " ticked")
        Move ("Rename " + String(iTicked) + " ticked") to sRename
        If (iTicked > 0) Begin
            Move ("Rename " + String(iTicked) + ", keep the other " + String(iRest)) to sKeep
            Move "Back up and rename the ticked copies to <name>.shadowed. The unticked ones stay on the board's line, to be looked at later." to sRenameTip
        End
        Else Begin
            Move ("Keep all " + String(iRest)) to sKeep
            Move "Nothing is ticked. Tick the copies to rename, keep the rest, or press Not now." to sRenameTip
        End
        If (iRest > 0) ;
            Move "The same rename for the ticked copies - and the unticked ones are recorded as KEPT forks, off the board's line until its kept chip offers them again." to sKeepTip
        Else ;
            Move "Every copy is ticked - there is nothing to keep." to sKeepTip
        Move (oWebBottomBar(Self)) to hoBar
        Move (oRenameBtn(hoBar)) to hoRename
        Move (oKeepBtn(hoBar)) to hoKeep
        Send UpdateCaption of hoRename sRename
        Send UpdateEnabled of hoRename (iTicked > 0)
        Send UpdateToolTip of hoRename sRenameTip
        Send UpdateCaption of hoKeep sKeep
        Send UpdateEnabled of hoKeep (iRest > 0)
        Send UpdateToolTip of hoKeep sKeepTip
        If (pbInitWebApp(hoBar) = False) ;
            Send CheckUpdateWebUI of hoBar

        /* RECOMMENDED follows the closers' rule: shut when a press would change nothing, with the reason in
           its tooltip (Nils 2026-10-05, on a workspace whose 14 copies all differed from the shipped files:
           "I'm not sure what the 'Recommended' button does? 0 is ticked if it is pressed?"). The recommended
           ticks are the ones the dialog opens with - TickIdenticalOnly's rule, counted here. */
        Move 0 to iRec
        Move True to bAsRec
        For i from 0 to (iRows - 1)
            Move (aRows[i].bSame or aRows[i].bAlways or aRows[i].bAddsNothingUsed) to bWant
            If (bWant = True) ;
                Increment iRec
            If (aRows[i].bTicked <> bWant) ;
                Move False to bAsRec
        Loop
        If (bAsRec = True and iRec = 0) ;
            Move "Nothing to recommend: none of these copies is identical to the file it stands in front of or shown to add nothing the workspace uses, so none is ticked for you. Compare a copy with that file before ticking it." to sRecTip
        Else If (bAsRec = True) ;
            Move ("The ticks are the recommended ones already: the " + String(iRec) + (If(iRec = 1, " copy", " copies")) + " a rename cannot cost anything.") to sRecTip
        Else If (iRec = 0) ;
            Move "Back to the recommended ticks. Here that is none: no copy is identical to the file it stands in front of or shown to add nothing the workspace uses." to sRecTip
        Else ;
            Move CS_RetireRecommendedTip to sRecTip
        Move (oWebSelectBar(Self)) to hoSelBar
        Move (oRecommendedBtn(hoSelBar)) to hoRec
        Send UpdateEnabled of hoRec (bAsRec = False)
        Send UpdateToolTip of hoRec sRecTip
        If (pbInitWebApp(hoSelBar) = False) ;
            Send CheckUpdateWebUI of hoSelBar
    End_Procedure

    /* Rename - and, with bKeepRest, keep the unticked. The array already holds the ticks: every tick
       path syncs it, and the closers sync once more inside their click. Not here - this runs after the
       click, from the click relay's timer, where a grid read faults (err 98). The disabled buttons cannot
       reach here with nothing to do - the guards stay anyway: a greyed button must not be the only thing
       between a user and a rename. */
    Procedure DoConfirm Boolean bKeepRest
        tShadowCopy[] aRows
        Integer iTicked iRest

        Get TickedCount to iTicked
        Get paRows to aRows
        Move (SizeOfArray(aRows) - iTicked) to iRest
        If (bKeepRest = False and iTicked = 0) Begin
            Send FTStopBox "Nothing is ticked. Tick the copies to rename, keep the rest, or press Not now." "Nothing to rename"
            Procedure_Return
        End
        If (bKeepRest = True and iRest = 0) Begin
            Send FTStopBox "Every copy is ticked - there is nothing to keep. Press Rename instead." "Nothing to keep"
            Procedure_Return
        End
        Set pbKeepRest to bKeepRest
        Set pbConfirmed to True
        Send Close_Panel
    End_Procedure

    Procedure DoCancel
        Set pbConfirmed to False
        Set pbKeepRest to False
        Send Close_Panel
    End_Procedure

    // Every Popup starts unconfirmed: the dialog object outlives one press, and a stale
    // pbConfirmed or pbKeepRest would read as consent the user never gave this time.
    Procedure Popup
        Set pbConfirmed to False
        Set pbKeepRest to False
        Forward Send Popup
    End_Procedure

    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_A  Send SelectAll    of oShadows_grd
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_N  Send SelectNone   of oShadows_grd
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_I  Send SelectInvert of oShadows_grd
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_C  Send DoCancel
End_Object

/*  THE ONE WAY IN. Hands the rows to the dialog, shows it, and returns True with each row's bTicked
    filled when the user pressed one of the two closers - bKeepRest says which: True means the
    unticked rows are to be recorded as kept. False, rows untouched, on Not now. The caller then
    renames exactly the ticked rows (cShadowedPackageFiles.RetireShadowCopies) and, when asked,
    remembers the rest (RememberKept). */
Function ChooseShadowCopiesToRetire Global tShadowCopy[] ByRef aRows Boolean ByRef bKeepRest Returns Boolean
    Handle ho
    Boolean bOk

    Move (oRetireShadows_dg(Self)) to ho
    Set paRows of ho to aRows
    Send Popup of ho
    Get pbConfirmed of ho to bOk
    Move False to bKeepRest
    If (bOk = True) Begin
        Get paRows of ho to aRows
        Get pbKeepRest of ho to bKeepRest
    End
    Function_Return bOk
End_Function
